Review this Rust function and explain the ownership bug, then give the smallest correct patch.
```rust
fn first_long_word(items: Vec<String>) -> &str {
    let mut best = "";
    for item in items {
        if item.len() > best.len() { best = &item; }
    }
    best
}
```
Keep the public intent unchanged.

Refactor this TypeScript API so invalid states are unrepresentable and exhaustive checking works.
```ts
type Job = { status: string; value?: string; error?: Error };
function render(job: Job): string {
  if (job.status === 'done') return job.value!;
  if (job.status === 'failed') return job.error!.message;
  return 'waiting';
}
```

Diagnose the race in this Java class and provide a minimal thread-safe replacement without serializing readers.
```java
final class Cache {
  private final Map<String, String> values = new HashMap<>();
  String get(String key) { return values.get(key); }
  void put(String key, String value) { values.put(key, value); }
}
```

Correct this Go function so timeout, goroutine lifetime, channel closure, and error propagation are all sound.
```go
func load(ctx context.Context) string {
    ch := make(chan string)
    go func() { ch <- slowRead() }()
    select {
    case value := <-ch: return value
    case <-time.After(time.Second): return ""
    }
}
```

Explain precisely why this C++ code has undefined behavior and rewrite it with a clear ownership contract.
```cpp
std::string_view label() {
    std::string value = compute_label();
    return value;
}
```
Also state one test that would fail nondeterministically in the original version.
